REDUNDANT WEB TIER
==================

Legend
  │ ▼   request path
  ╎ ▲   response path
  ┌─┐   component
  ╔═╗   boundary of one web/application node (one machine per node)
  ◀     remaining single point of failure


    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │                           User                           │
    └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
              │                                 ▲
              │ Request over TCP/IP             ╎ Response over TCP/IP
              ▼                                 ╎
    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐              ┌────────────────────┐
    │                      www.foobar.com                      │──── lookup ─▶│        DNS         │
    │                                                          │◀╌╌╌ 8.8.8.8 ╌│                    │
    └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘              └────────────────────┘
              │                                 ▲
              │ A record → 8.8.8.8              ╎ Response
              ▼                                 ╎
    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │                 Load balancer (HAProxy)                  │ ◀ remaining SPOF
    └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                │                                   │
                │ round robin                       │ round robin
                │                                   │
                ▼                                   ▼
╔════════════════════════════════╗  ╔════════════════════════════════╗
║  Web/App node 1                ║  ║  Web/App node 2                ║
║                                ║  ║                                ║
║  ┌──────────────────────────┐  ║  ║  ┌──────────────────────────┐  ║
║  │    Web server (Nginx)    │  ║  ║  │    Web server (Nginx)    │  ║
║  └──────────────────────────┘  ║  ║  └──────────────────────────┘  ║
║               │                ║  ║               │                ║
║               │ reverse proxy  ║  ║               │ reverse proxy  ║
║               ▼                ║  ║               ▼                ║
║  ┌──────────────────────────┐  ║  ║  ┌──────────────────────────┐  ║
║  │    Application server    │  ║  ║  │    Application server    │  ║
║  └──────────────────────────┘  ║  ║  └──────────────────────────┘  ║
║               │                ║  ║               │                ║
║               │ runs           ║  ║               │ runs           ║
║               ▼                ║  ║               ▼                ║
║  ┌──────────────────────────┐  ║  ║  ┌──────────────────────────┐  ║
║  │     Application code     │  ║  ║  │     Application code     │  ║
║  └──────────────────────────┘  ║  ║  └──────────────────────────┘  ║
║                                ║  ║                                ║
╚════════════════════════════════╝  ╚════════════════════════════════╝
                │                                   │
                │ reads / writes                    │ reads / writes
                ▼                                   ▼
    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │                 Database primary (MySQL)                 │ ◀ remaining SPOF
    └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                 │
                                 │ replication
                                 ▼
    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │                 Database replica (MySQL)                 │ read-only, no writes
    └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘


Notes
  - Both nodes receive traffic at the same time, so the pair is
    active-active rather than active-passive.
  - Responses retrace the same route in reverse: primary -> application
    code -> application server -> web server -> balancer -> user.
  - Every read and every write is sent to the primary. The replica
    receives a one-way stream of changes and accepts no writes.
  - Nothing in this design promotes the replica on its own. Replication
    protects the data, not the ability to keep writing.
  - Name resolution happens before the connection is opened and is not a
    hop on the way to the balancer.
  - The rendered version of this design is redundant_web_tier.png.
